Directory Breakdown
Root Level

    CMakeLists.txt: Build configuration file for compiling the project using CMake.
    README.md: Contains project description, setup instructions, and usage guidelines.
    LICENSE: Licensing information for the project.

docs/

Documentation related to the project.

    architecture/: Detailed architectural diagrams and explanations.
    api/: API documentation generated from code comments.
    user_guides/: Manuals and guides for users and developers.

configs/

Configuration files for various components.

    exchange_configs/: Connection and authentication details for exchanges.
    strategy_configs/: Parameters and settings for trading strategies.
    risk_configs/: Risk thresholds and rules definitions.

include/

Header files organized similarly to the src/ directory for clarity and separation.

    common/: Shared utilities and definitions across modules.
    market_data/: Interfaces and definitions for market data handling.
    ...

src/

Source code of the project.

    main.cpp: The entry point of the application.
    common/: Common utilities, constants, and helper functions.
        utils.cpp/h: General utility functions used across the system.
    market_data/: Market Data Handler component.
        market_data_handler.cpp/h: Core functionalities for handling market data.
        adapters/: Exchange-specific adapters to normalize data.
            binance_adapter.cpp: Adapter for Binance exchange.
            coinbase_adapter.cpp: Adapter for Coinbase exchange.
        protocols/: Implementations of communication protocols.
            websocket_client.cpp/h: WebSocket client implementation.
            rest_client.cpp/h: REST API client implementation.
    strategy/: Strategy Engine component.
        strategy_engine.cpp/h: Core logic for executing strategies.
        strategies/: Individual trading strategies.
            mean_reversion.cpp/h: Mean reversion strategy implementation.
            momentum.cpp/h: Momentum trading strategy.
        backtesting/: Tools for backtesting strategies.
            backtester.cpp/h: Backtesting engine.
            test_data/: Sample historical data for testing.
    oms/: Order Management System.
        oms.cpp/h: Core OMS functionalities.
        order_execution/: Handles order submissions.
            order_executor.cpp/h: Logic for executing orders.
        order_tracking/: Tracks order statuses.
            order_tracker.cpp/h: Monitors orders from submission to execution.
        exchange_interfaces/: Interfaces to different exchanges.
            binance_interface.cpp/h
            coinbase_interface.cpp/h
    risk_management/: Risk Management Module.
        risk_manager.cpp/h: Core risk management logic.
        pre_trade_checks/: Pre-trade validation checks.
            checks.cpp/h: Implements various risk checks.
        position_monitoring/: Monitors open positions and exposures.
            position_monitor.cpp/h
        risk_rules/: Defines risk management rules.
            risk_rule_base.cpp/h: Base class for risk rules.
    connectivity/: Connectivity Layer.
        network_manager.cpp/h: Manages network connections.
        protocols/: Network protocols implementations.
            fix_client.cpp/h: FIX protocol client.
            protocol_definitions.h: Protocol constants and definitions.
    data_storage/: Data Storage and Retrieval.
        storage_manager.cpp/h: Manages data read/write operations.
        real_time_data/: Handles real-time data storage.
            real_time_db.cpp/h
        historical_data/: Manages historical data access.
            historical_db.cpp/h
        serialization/: Data serialization and deserialization.
            serializer.cpp/h
    monitoring/: Monitoring and Logging System.
        monitoring.cpp/h: Core monitoring functionalities.
        logging/: Logging mechanisms.
            logger.cpp/h: Implements logging functionalities using spdlog.
        metrics/: Collects and reports metrics.
            metrics_collector.cpp/h
        alerts/: Alerting system.
            alert_manager.cpp/h

tests/

Test suites for ensuring code quality.

    unit_tests/: Unit tests for individual components.
        test_market_data_handler.cpp: Tests for the Market Data Handler.
        test_strategy_engine.cpp: Tests for the Strategy Engine.
    integration_tests/: Tests that cover end-to-end scenarios.
        test_end_to_end.cpp: Simulates full trading cycles.

scripts/

Auxiliary scripts for deployment, setup, and utilities.

    deploy.sh: Script for deploying the application.
    setup_env.sh: Sets up the development environment.
    utils/: Utility scripts.
        data_cleanup.py: Cleans up old data files.
        log_rotate.sh: Rotates log files.

third_party/

Third-party libraries and dependencies that are not managed via package managers.

    boost/: Boost libraries if not using system-installed versions.
    spdlog/: Logging library.
    ...

resources/

Static resources required by the application.

    ssl_certificates/: SSL/TLS certificates for secure connections.
    sample_configs/: Example configuration files for reference.

Additional Notes

    Modularity: Each major component has its own directory within src/ and include/, making it easier to navigate and maintain.
    Separation of Concerns: By dividing code into logical directories, developers can work on different components with minimal conflicts.
    Reusability: Common utilities and definitions are placed in common/ to be accessible by all components.
    Scalability: The structure allows for easy addition of new exchanges, strategies, or risk rules by adding new files or directories in the appropriate place.
    Testing: Dedicated directories for unit and integration tests ensure that all code changes are properly verified.
    Configuration Management: Placing configuration files in configs/ allows for dynamic adjustments without altering the codebase.
